# QVAC SDK

Package: `@qvac/sdk`. Runtimes: **Node.js** and **Bare**. Docs:
https://docs.qvac.tether.io — for agents, https://docs.qvac.tether.io/llms-full.txt

Sibling `fibiom-electron` shows a working Electron integration. Copy **SDK
usage**, not the app: `loadModel` / `completion` / `embed` / `transcribe` /
`unloadModel`, streaming events, tool loops, plugin tree-shaking.

## Lifecycle (req 1.3–1.4)

`loadModel` → inference (`completion` / `embed` / `transcribe` / TTS) →
`unloadModel` → `close`. Cancel in-flight loads and completions by
`requestId`.

## Models (req 1.2, 5.2)

Discover/download from at least two of: QVAC registry
(`modelRegistryList` / `modelRegistrySearch`), filesystem, HTTPS, `pear://`.
Select model and quantization at runtime from device capability
(`getSystemResources`, `assessModelFit`). Default to something that can live
on 8 GB RAM.

## RAG (req 2)

`ragChunk()` + `embed()` into a persistent local vector store (SQLite-Vector,
LanceDB, Chroma, or similar). Schema dimensionality must match the embedding
model. Stream tokens. Attach citations (`file` relative to corpus root).

## Tools (req 3)

Load a **tool-capable** model. Declare tools with **Zod** schemas in the
`tools` array on `completion()`. Drive the loop from structured tool-call
events — do not regex-scrape model text. Required: `list_documents`; stock
lookup from the provided `stock-tool.zip`.

## Voice, vision, P2P (req 4–5)

ASR via whispercpp and/or parakeet (`transcribe` and/or `transcribeStream`).
Hands-free: speech → grounded answer → TTS. Image + text in one VLM context.
P2P: `startQVACProvider()` on the strong machine;
`loadModel({ delegate: { providerPublicKey, fallbackToLocal: true } })` on
the field laptop.

## Footprint (req 6.2–6.3)

Declare only used plugins/addons in `qvac.config.*`. Produce a tree-shaken
build. Reuse KV cache across turns with a per-session key.
